{{wikipedia}}
==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|enm}} {{term|laumprei|lang=enm}}, adopted from {{etyl|fro}} {{term|lampreie|lang=fro}} (Modern ''[[lamproie]]''), from {{etyl|ML.}} ''[[lampreda]]'', possibly from {{etyl|LL.}} ''[[lampetra]]'', from a combination of ''[[lambere]]'' ("lick") + ''[[petra]]'' ("stone").

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈlæm.pɹi/}}
* {{hyphenation|lam|prey}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}
[[Image:Havsnejonöga.jpg|right|thumb|A '''lamprey''']]

# Any long slender [[primitive]] eel-like [[freshwater]] and saltwater [[fish]] of the ''[[Petromyzontidae]]'' [[family]], having a [[sucking]] [[mouth]] with [[rasping]] [[teeth]] but no [[jaw]].

====Derived terms====
* [[brook lamprey]]
* [[European river lamprey]]
* [[sea lamprey]]

